IMO, polymorphing gives you 2 lives. When the monster you have become "dies"
ie HP =< 0 you revert to your "normal" character with full HP. I don't think
you can stay a monster permanantly. In my experience with poly and poly 
control rings i can keep choosing to be one kind of monster if i wishes, but
should i take the poly ring off i would revert back sooner or later. I think
it works the same for polymorph wand, chameleon corpse and poly traps. 
A cockatrice for a pet is not that adventageous as far as finding food is 
concerned. Neither is a HP(345) pet dragon who swoops and consumes that much
needed morsel...
For monsters, pets included, the change is permanant until the next time it
get zapped or stepped on a poly trap...and it does not revert to the original
animal...

